course: dictionary
lesson: 4788
title: Kind words in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Context means the words around a word, and they leave clues. «Mice prefer grains, seeds and sweet foods to cheese, so peanut butter works better in humane traps.» The sentence is about catching mice without hurting them, so humane must mean kind and gentle.
explain: Humane means kind and gentle, causing as little pain as possible to people or animals. Check your guess by swapping it into the sentence: a kind and gentle trap that causes as little pain as possible still makes sense, so you have it.
explain: Humane often appears in phrases such as humane treatment and a humane trap. The words next to it, like treatment or trap, show you what kind of kindness is meant.
fact: Humane means kind and gentle, causing as little pain as possible to people or animals.
fact: «A humane trap» is a trap that catches an animal without hurting it.
fact: «Humane treatment» means kind care for people or animals.
fact: Humane is an adjective, so it describes a noun, such as a trap or a way. Its comparative form is more humane.
exercise: «Mice prefer grains, seeds and sweet foods to cheese, so peanut butter works better in humane traps.» What does humane mean here? | Very large | Fast and noisy | *Kind and gentle, causing as little pain as possible | Cruel and harsh
exercise: What does humane treatment mean? | Ignoring someone who is hurt | *Kind care that causes as little pain as possible | Throwing away litter | Loud shouting at an animal
exercise: In «a humane way to catch a mouse», what does humane describe? | The mouse | The cheese | The grains | *The way of catching
test: «In history, the king passed humane laws to protect the poor.» What does humane suggest about these laws? | They were loud and very long | They were broken quickly | *They were fair and kind | They were made by mice
test: Which word is the best swap for humane in «a humane trap» that catches a mouse without hurting it? | Harsh | Huge | Noisy | *Gentle
exam: Which sentence uses humane correctly? | The dog was humane, so it bit everyone in the park | The sky was humane and blue all day | *The vet gave the sick cat humane care, with no more pain than needed | The humane was very fast on the track
